I have compressed the >900K binary with pfxpak to about 550K, and I am
currently doing ok with 4Megs, one 720K floppy and one 320K floppy (!).
The other floppy is only for loading 512K RAM-disk (with all data and
level files) into memory and for Save-files, so one 720K should be enough.
Also 2Megs memory should be enough, even with RAM-disk.

What bothers me in this ST-port is that colors are behaving really wierd
and also some screen updates are not working (inventory draws and white
line on the screen and score board shows only one line before switching
text to white-on-white-background.) I hope that the official release
will fix this small machine-specific problems, as it is fun game :)

